Fuzzer scenario profiles
------------------------
Each *.lua file here is a scenario the rr fuzz harness (nerfhack-rr-fuzz.sh)
rotates through: the game runs the chosen profile on turn 1 and again on the
first turn after every level change (NH_FUZZER_SETUP, see
fuzzer_setup_script() in wizcmds.c), so a profile seeds every level the hero
visits with the objects, monsters and traps whose code it wants exercised,
and seeds the hero once (guard the run-once part with nh.variable(), which
persists across runs).  Anything the random keystroke fuzzer would only reach
by luck -- a monster wearing an artifact, a corpse frozen in a monster's ice
box, a lit lamp in a monster's pack -- belongs in a profile.

The scripts run in the same sandbox as #wizloadlua: des.*, obj.*, u.giveobj,
nh.random, nh.variable, nh.pline.  A script error is an impossible(), which
panics under the fuzzer, so a broken profile shows up as a crash in every
session that uses it rather than silently seeding nothing.  Each profile
prints "fuzz profile: <name> seeded" so a session log shows it ran.

Ending the game
---------------
The fuzzer life-saves the hero through every death and doup() refuses to
climb out of dungeon level 1, so nothing after done() -- disclosure, the
dumplog (text and HTML), tombstone, topten, freeing everything at exit --
runs unless a profile asks for it:
  nh.fuzz_die(pct)   from now on let pct percent of deaths stand (the
                     wizard-mode "Die?" prompt is answered for the fuzzer)
  nh.fuzz_escape()   take the hero to dungeon level 1, put it on the up
                     staircase and climb via the real #up command (after
                     50 failed tries -- rooted, held, overloaded -- the
                     game is ended directly)
Both are per process: a restored session starts with them off until the
profile runs again (it does, on the first turn after the restore).  The
harness sets NH_FUZZER_DUMPLOG so the dump files are written next to the
session's trace; a cleanly ended session's dumplog.txt/.html are kept in
fuzz-sessions/dumplogs/ and the summary line says end=died|escaped.
See gameover.lua.
